      "title": "Barnaby Joyce claims One Nation ‘one of the gayest parties in Australia’ as former candidate’s comments surface",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/12/barnaby-joyce-one-nation-paraminder-singh-homophobic-comments-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>One Nation MP says failed WA candidate’s comments describing same-sex attraction as a mental illness are ‘highly offensive’</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Barnaby Joyce has defended One Nation as “one of the gayest parties in Australia” after comments surfaced from one of its failed candidates describing same-sex attraction as a mental illness.</p><p>The former National turned One Nation MP was asked to respond to a series of homophobic comments made by a former Western Australian legislative council candidate for One Nation in a video last month, <a href=\"https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-08-12/parminder-singh-one-nation-parminder-singh/107027568\">as first reported by ABC</a> on Wednesday afternoon.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/12/barnaby-joyce-one-nation-paraminder-singh-homophobic-comments-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-12T10:13:18"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘Send food photos’: Lobbyist paid for former premier’s brother to go to Fiji to avoid inquiry, Icac hears",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/12/members-of-liberal-group-received-kickbacks-from-lobbying-companys-catholic-schools-nsw-contract-icac-hears-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Lobbyist Jeremy Greenwood gives evidence about allegations linked to Reformers at Independent Commission Against Corruption hearing</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A Liberal figure under investigation for allegedly accepting illegal political donations has told an inquiry he paid for the brother of former premier Dominic Perrottet to travel to Fiji and urged the CEO of Catholic Schools NSW to “go to Brisbane” to avoid appearing before a parliamentary committee.</p><p>Consultant and lobbyist Jeremy Greenwood gave his third day of evidence to the Independent Commission Against Corruption’s (Icac) Operation Rosny on Wednesday.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/12/members-of-liberal-group-received-kickbacks-from-lobbying-companys-catholic-schools-nsw-contract-icac-hears-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-12T09:31:19"
    },
    {
      "title": "O’Neil condemns Bragg’s ‘crazed’ press club speech – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/12/australia-politics-live-question-time-anthony-albanese-angus-taylor-coalition-andrew-bragg-housing-construction-immigration-one-nation-pauline-hanson-gambling-melon-gift-japan-ndis-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>This blog is now closed</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Education minister says funding agreement with Victoria ‘very close’</strong></p><p>The education minister, <strong>Jason Clare</strong>, says a funding deal with Victoria to get public schools funded to Gonski levels over the next decade is “very close”.</p><p>We’re very close, mate. I know [Victorian premier] <strong>Ben Carroll</strong> gets this, and I’m optimistic that we’ll get this across the line. He understands how important it is that teachers are paid well, that they do the best or do the most important job in the country, but how important it is that we fix the funding of our schools – we’ve struck agreements now, 10-year agreements, with every state and territory across the country except Victoria. We’re very close to landing that deal.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/12/australia-politics-live-question-time-anthony-albanese-angus-taylor-coalition-andrew-bragg-housing-construction-immigration-one-nation-pauline-hanson-gambling-melon-gift-japan-ndis-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-12T08:43:05"
    },
    {
      "title": "Japanese ambassador to Australia downplays Albanese melon gaffe as Taylor claims PM has ‘stuffed up’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/12/anthony-albanese-japanese-prime-minister-melon-gate-coalition",
      "description": "<p>Coalition demands police investigate apparent leaking of diplomatic cable to newspaper but Labor calls it a ‘silly political stunt’</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/12/australia-politics-live-question-time-anthony-albanese-angus-taylor-coalition-andrew-bragg-housing-construction-immigration-one-nation-pauline-hanson-gambling-melon-gift-japan-ndis-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The Japanese ambassador has downplayed Anthony Albanese’s comments about a gift of melons from Sanae Takaichi, saying Tokyo had been reassured by the Australian government that the prime minister “did not make the comments in the way that has been reported”.</p><p>While the Coalition continued to raise outrage over Albanese’s comments to the Bush Deep podcast, including seeking to have federal police investigate the alleged leaking of a diplomatic cable to a newspaper, the Japanese government appeared to be uninterested in making a diplomatic incident out of the much-maligned comments.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/12/anthony-albanese-japanese-prime-minister-melon-gate-coalition\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-12T08:18:06"
    },
